"heptapod@gmail.com" <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
> I keep hitting this button by accident, it kicks me out to the terminal.

That was actually a feature, a long long time ago. :-)

Spawning a shell process from within NetHack allowed you to quickly
check your mail or do something that resembled work. But of course
that was when you only had a hardware terminal and not multiple xterm
windows in your X11 session (so it's been obsolete for quite some time
already).

On public servers this is *usually* disabled but there have been cases
where it hasn't been.

> How do I get back into my game,

Just type 'exit' and press enter.

> or is my game lost forever? How do I
> disable the !? What do I comment out of the source?

In include/config.h, comment out the following line:
#define SHELL                /* do not delete the '!' command */

